# APML: Node Home — THE VIEW's one recursive dashboard
# Last updated: 2026-08-07 (state_badge: a trial names its LANGUAGE, not the raw course code,
#               and a trial school records that language at its first class — B1;
#               school-admin first-run affordances on the member mount;
#               creator becomes first manager; the node names its leader;
#               duplicate-name warning on Add-a-group and on Rename;
#               password gate + PWA install nudge before an org manager's first add;
#               permanent "Your account" card — the same two actions, always reachable)
# Contract: docs/THE-VIEW.md (founder-ruled 2026-07-19) — companion to docs/THE-MODEL.md

dressing:  # founder ruling 2026-08-02 ("orgs are groups all the way down")
  presets: neutral (group / group leader / learner — the DEFAULT) · education (school / teacher / class / student)
  derivation: |
    composables/nodeTerminology.ts derives the preset from the payload — a
    subtree renders the education vocabulary iff it actually carries school
    DNA (school attachment / commercial, teacher or class rollups, a school
    above or below in the rail). No stored preset, no second ontology:
    existing school orgs keep their words with zero migration; a fresh org
    (Cardiff Council) renders neutral until a school genuinely exists in it.
  neutral_effects: |
    stats row = practice hours · groups · learners (never teacher/class
    tiles); lenses reduced to directly-below + all-groups; Add-a-school verb
    hidden; invite roles = group leader (default) + learner; children-list
    rows count groups+learners (per-row derivation in NodeChildrenList);
    How-this-works serves the 'org' explanations from the pack.
  chrome_badge: |
    the header-chrome role badge for a govt_admin routes through
    nodeTerminology.leaderRoleLabel() (neutral default 'Group Leader') —
    'Govt Admin' was a dressing leak (founder bug 2026-08-02: Cardiff
    Council's leader badged as government staff). Chrome has no node payload
    to derive a preset from, so it takes the neutral default.
  follow_up: an EXPLICIT stored preset (org chooses education vocabulary
    before any school exists) is known follow-up, not built.

purpose: |
  One page — the NODE HOME — with the same grammar at every level of the org
  tree, replacing the three-designs era (group summary page / Full-schools
  list / Structure panel as separate dashboards). Total clarity about what
  you're in and where you're looking: a MAP of the org with a visual
  you-are-here at every level.

surface:
  route_group: /admin/groups/:id      # node home for a group node (index)
  route_school: /admin/schools/:id    # node home for a school's node (index; deep tools stay at sub-routes)
  route_class: /admin/classes/:id     # node home at class level (AdminClassHome shell)
  redirect_full_schools_list: "/admin/groups/:id/schools -> /admin/groups/:id?lens=schools"
  route_member: /schools/org/:id      # MEMBER mount (2026-07-20): a leader's node home inside the
                                      # /schools shell — ONE :id route for groups, schools AND classes
                                      # (the endpoint resolves the kind); + /schools/org/:id/insights.
                                      # Server-scoped to the leader's own subtree; rail rooted at their
                                      # top node (no "All organisations" admin escape); verbs = the
                                      # invite pair + Add-a-group (2026-08-02: POST /api/groups
                                      # authorizes a leader on their own subtree; root creation is
                                      # self-serve for any signed-in user, creator becomes leader);
                                      # links derived per-mount via composables/nodeSurfacePaths.ts.
                                      # Landing: DashboardView redirects a govt_admin with a group_id
                                      # to /schools/org/:group_id (legacy region-only leaders keep the
                                      # old group dashboard).

grammar:  # the same five parts, every level (THE-VIEW §1)
  map_rail: NodeMapRail.vue           # ancestors root→here, you-are-here lit, siblings toggle, children below
  identity_header: node name + label badge + demo/trial/paid state; class level adds read-only teachers (lead first)
  state_badge: |
    NodeHomeView.vue::stateBadge — demo · paid ("Paid — all courses") ·
    trial · any other platform_status verbatim (underscores spaced).

    A TRIAL badge NAMES THE LANGUAGE, never the raw course code:
    "Trial — Welsh (South)", off courseShortName(commercial.trialCourseCode)
    from @ssi/core (packages/core/src/courses/displayName.ts). That helper is
    the ONE source of truth for course labels — do not add another hardcoded
    list here (the repo already carries three: lib/teacherCourses.ts,
    composables/schools/useSchoolCourseCatalogue.ts, insight/data/demo.ts,
    and that duplication is what produced this bug).

    A trial with NO course recorded reads a bare "Trial". That is now a
    genuinely transient state — a trial school records its language the
    moment it creates its first class with a course
    (api/_utils/schoolPlatformTrial.ts::ensureSchoolTrialCourse, called from
    POST /api/teacher/create-class-learner). Before that fix, an invite-born
    school (redeem.ts has no course to pass at redemption) stayed null
    forever and the badge was a permanent blank — founder report 2026-08-07,
    the Chepstow school.
  stats_row: learners · teachers · classes · practice hours — SUBTREE totals via groupRollups.computeNodeExtras
  children_list: NodeChildrenList.vue # one row grammar for every lens payload
  verbs: invite someone (role × node) · see insights · quick actions (Structure flyout)
  # Add-a-group WARNS on a duplicate name (2026-08-06). A sibling under THIS
  # node whose name slugs to the same string makes POST /api/groups answer 409
  # { code: 'duplicate_name' } and create nothing; NodeActionBar shows which
  # group already exists and when, and offers "Change the name" or "Go ahead
  # anyway" — the latter re-sends with confirm_duplicate: true. Warning only:
  # legitimate duplicates are allowed once a human has said so. Scope is
  # same-parent, so a "Year 7" under a different school never warns. The
  # RENAME verb warns the same way off PATCH /api/groups/:id — same 409, same
  # two ways out, and never about the row being renamed itself. Full
  # contract: apml/core/roles-and-permissions.apml duplicate_name_warning.
  manager_onboarding_gate: |
    An ORG MANAGER must set a password BEFORE their first add (founder ruling
    2026-08-06, off Deborah's question on the org lane: "Password before
    adding a group or a learner? and then once they've done that, a context
    aware install as PWA, on a desktop likely to be a chrome app").

    WHY: a manager arrives by magic link, lands in their organisation and
    simply stays signed in. They never set a password, so when that session
    dies — new device, cleared storage, a phone reset — there is no way back
    into the organisation they just built.

    PRESENTED AS TWO GUIDED WALK-THROUGHS (founder taste call 2026-08-06
    22:38Z, binding on the UX): "not a bare form or a naked prompt" — each is
    a PURPOSE SENTENCE FIRST, then under five paced steps to done, in the
    walkthrough engine's own card genre. The genre is shared LITERALLY via
    components/admin/WalkCard.vue, extracted from WalkOverlay.vue in the same
    pass, so there is one teaching voice rather than two lookalikes.
      · password walk: why (you came in by a link that will not last) → the
        two fields → done. Three beats, no escape on any of them.
      · install walk: why (context-aware by device) → do it. Two beats,
        escapable throughout.
    WHY IT IS NOT AN ENGINE WALK — the engine is an INVITATION system: it
    never auto-plays (compile gate 7 makes startWalk-outside-@click a build
    failure), never traps the page, and anchors to elements already on screen.
    The password step fires unbidden, blocks, and has no skip. Routing it
    through the engine would have meant breaking the never-auto-play gate,
    which is load-bearing. It therefore borrows the genre, not the mechanism.
    RESOLVED 2026-08-06 (founder ruling): the durable anchor is now
    `your_account` below. The gate itself is UNCHANGED — it remains the front
    door for a brand-new manager — and the same two actions are additionally
    registered as real pack walks against the permanent surface, so
    How-this-works offers them like every other feature.

    TWO BEATS, deliberately different in kind:
      1. PASSWORD — a GATE. No skip, no close. Intercepts the three verbs a
         manager holds (Invite a person · Get a shareable link · Add a group),
         all of which pass through NodeActionBar's single toggle() choke
         point. On success the intercepted verb RESUMES immediately — the
         manager never has to find the button again.
      2. INSTALL — a PROMPT, not a gate. Context-aware by device
         (utils/installPlatform.ts): desktop Chrome says "Chrome app", other
         desktops say "app", phones say "home screen". Always escapable
         ("Not now"), dismissal remembered per user in localStorage, skipped
         entirely when already running standalone. Routes to the existing
         /install walkthrough carrying ?return=<current path> so the manager
         lands back on their own node, never the learner home.

    SCOPE — needsPasswordGate(member && leadsOrg && !hasPassword):
      · `member` = the /org member mount, never the ssi_admin god-view.
      · `leadsOrg` = useOrgLeadership's server-verified 'organisation' leader
        row. This is what keeps the gate OUT of the schools lane: /org/:id
        renders school nodes on the same member mount, so `member` alone would
        leak it. School admins, teachers and learners are untouched.
      · `hasPassword` reads user_metadata.has_password — the same flag
        SettingsScreen reads and useAuth.updatePassword writes. A MISSING flag
        counts as no password: the safe direction, since the worst case is a
        manager setting a password they already had. KNOWN LIMIT — that flag
        is only ever written by our own updatePassword, and Supabase exposes
        no server-side "this user has a password" signal on the session user.
      · Validation mirrors SettingsScreen exactly (6 characters, confirm must
        match); a longer server-side minimum surfaces in Supabase's own words.
    Surfaces: components/admin/ManagerOnboardingGate.vue (both beats),
    composables/useManagerOnboarding.ts (decision logic),
    utils/installPlatform.ts (detection + framing, shared with InstallGuide).

  your_account: |
    THE PERMANENT HOME for the same two actions (founder ruling 2026-08-06):
    "a leader can set/change their password and install the app AT ANY TIME,
    not just at first login". components/admin/YourAccount.vue, last card on
    the node home, after Ways in — Ways in is how OTHER people get in, this is
    how YOU get back in.

    SCOPE: the member mount only (`member && !isClass && home.node`). On the
    admin mount an ssi_admin is looking at someone else's node, and their own
    account is not what that page is about. No leadsOrg round trip: /org/* IS
    the leader lane, and a permanent dismissible card is not a gate, so the
    tighter predicate the GATE needs would only buy a request.

    NOTHING RE-IMPLEMENTED — the password uses useManagerOnboarding's
    validatePassword + useAuth.updatePassword, the install uses
    installPlatform's detectFromBrowser + installFraming. If the gate's rules
    change, this changes with them. The copy adapts: "No password yet / Set a
    password" before, "Password / Change it" after; the install row says
    Chrome app · app · home screen by device, and goes quiet with "The app is
    installed" when already standalone. A link-auth placeholder address is
    never displayed as if it were an inbox (utils/placeholderEmail.ts).

    WALK ANCHORS on the ROW containers, never the buttons: account-card ·
    account-password · account-install. The install row has no button once
    installed, so a button-mounted anchor would vanish exactly when the walk
    still wants to point at it. Pack walks set-your-password and
    install-the-app (personas: leader) are anchored here and offered from
    How-this-works — that is what makes these two actions covered features
    rather than a one-time flow.
  # The admin "Class tools" page is DEAD (founder ruling 2026-07-19): it
  # duplicated the class node home with zero admin-usable verbs. Its route
  # (/admin/schools/:id/classes/:classId) redirects to /admin/classes/:classId.
  student_rows: |
    FLAT (founder ruling 2026-07-19): all per-student teaching data on the one
    row, no click — health dot, last practised, course-journey bar (LEGOs done
    of course total), belt, LEGOs, practice hours, last-7-days sparkline +
    week minutes. No expansion panel, no individual learner page, and NO
    STREAKS anywhere (docs/gamification-done-right.md). On phone the row
    wraps: stats strip + journey bar under the name (sparkline hidden).

lenses:  # filters over the one view, never separate pages; ?lens= in the URL
  children: direct child nodes (default)
  groups: every group below, all the way down
  schools: every school below, with teacher names
  teachers: every teacher below, with their classes
  classes: every class below, with student counts + hours
  students: fixed lens at class level

ordering:  # founder ruling 2026-07-30: "the schools are listed in a different
           # order from the groups and the everything directly below" — ONE
           # consistent order everywhere. rail siblings/children, every lens
           # list (children/groups/schools/teachers/classes) and the class
           # students roster are all alphabetical by name (locale-aware,
           # case-insensitive, numeric-aware — api/_utils/alphaSort.ts,
           # mirrored client-side at packages/player-vue/src/utils/alphaSort.ts).
           # Practice hours/student counts still show as row columns; they no
           # longer drive order. A metric order stays available ONLY where
           # it's an explicit, visible user choice (e.g. SchoolsView.vue's
           # labelled "Sort by hours/students/name" control, default name) —
           # never a silent default that can drift from a sibling list.
  default: alphabetical, every structural/navigational list
  metric_orders_must_be: explicit AND visible (a labelled sort control), never silent

data:
  endpoint: GET /api/groups/:id/home?lens=<lens>   # api/groups/[id]/home.ts
  id_resolution: group node id | school id (schools.node_group_id, minted on demand) | class id → kind 'class'
  authz: resolveGroupTreeCaller + callerCanSeeGroup; leader scope-trims ancestors/siblings to own subtree
  rollups: shared resolver (api/_utils/groupRollups.computeNodeExtras) — same story as tree/table lenses
  subtree_membership: parent_id walk (api/_utils/groupSubtree.descendantIds), NEVER the slug path —
    compute_group_path() slugifies the name and nothing makes it unique, so two same-named orgs
    shared one path live (2026-08-06) and each one's rollup swallowed the other's people
  leaders: who leads THIS node — govt_admins ∪ the leader membership tag
    (user_tags tag_type='group', role_in_context='admin'), names resolved via learners.
    Founder ruling 2026-08-06: the creator of a group/org IS its first manager. Before
    this, leadership lived only in govt_admins — which no lens reads — so a creator
    governed a group whose page showed no manager anywhere while the ways-in ledger
    right below it printed their own name against the link they had minted.
    Rendered "Led by <names>"; a root with no leader says "No group leader yet"
    rather than rendering nothing (an absent line and an absent leader looked identical).
  practice_hours: subtree school_summary sum (incl. staff practice)
    + directly group-attached people's sessions (api/_utils/directMemberPractice.ts) — a group whose
      people were invited straight in (user_tags tag_type='group', no school, no class) has no
      school_summary row, so without this term it reported 0h forever while learnerCount said 1+,
      and the explainer's org-not-started rule told its leader nobody had practised
    - excludes anyone already reachable through a subtree school/class (no double count)
    class level sums class_student_progress

layout_stability:  # founder bug 2026-07-20 — "3-4 up and down page wobbles" per rail switch
  # While a load runs, every section HOLDS its geometry; VALUES never show the wrong node.
  - node switch (id changed): identity/stats/class-card/action-bar value slots blank to nbsp
    but keep their boxes; the children body holds its pre-load height (measured min-height)
    instead of collapsing to a spinner line; ONE settle when the new node's data lands
  - same-node refresh / lens change: identity+stats keep their still-correct numbers
    (stale-while-refreshing); only the children body holds
  - action bar goes visibility:hidden mid-switch so a click can never act on the previous node
  - AdminGroupContainer's entity-context-bar stays MOUNTED once painted (its unmount/remount
    was the biggest measured shifter); the group name blanks while loading
  - the map rail keeps its previous tree until arrival (continuity ruling) and swaps once
  - probe: packages/player-vue/e2e/the-view/layout-stability-probe.mjs (CLS + section height
    timeline per switch, deployed build; target CLS/switch < 0.02 incl. input-adjacent shifts)

rail_stability:  # founder finding 2026-07-30 — hopping Overview <-> Insights faked a full screen load
  # NodeHomeView and NodeInsightsView are separate route components that each fetch
  # /api/groups/:id/home; the hop used to remount the rail column empty (v-if on the
  # payload) and re-fetch, flashing intermediate text in the WHERE-YOU-ARE column.
  mechanism: composables/admin/nodeHomeCache.ts   # keyed cache, NOT a shared-layout route refactor
  tiers:
    - in-memory full payload, keyed route-id + lens (page lifetime): the sibling view
      seeds it, so the next view paints the WHOLE page synchronously on a warm hop —
      the remount is invisible; the fresh fetch reconciles silently in the background
    - sessionStorage rail subset (ancestors/node/siblings/children/kind only), keyed
      route-id: full page reload rehydrates the tree with no identity flash; stats and
      rollups are never persisted — they come fresh or show a loading state
  rules:
    - the rail COLUMN always renders; a genuinely cold node (nothing cached) gets
      NodeMapRailSkeleton.vue — quiet grey bars, never explainer text, and the main
      pane never slides into the rail column
    - honesty: cache keys on route id + lens so the wrong node/lens is never served;
      a non-OK /home response drops the node's cache (a stale rail can't outlive
      lost access); the background refetch always reconciles to fresh
    - the rail's siblings-open toggle persists per node id across remounts
      (module-level state in NodeMapRail.vue) — the tree never visibly resets on a hop
  tests: NodeInsightsView.test.ts (warm-hop / cold-skeleton / honesty pins) +
    NodeHomeView.test.ts RAIL-STABILITY PIN + nodeHomeCache.test.ts

rail_everywhere:  # founder ruling 2026-07-31 — "everyone should know where they are in the
  # breadcrumb, even if they can't go UP a level because of permissions … I don't like the
  # LHS anchor just disappearing." The rail is ORIENTATION, not navigation: EVERY
  # /schools-shell view keeps it, including the flat (non-node-surface) pages.
  mechanism: SchoolsContainer wraps meta.railFrame routes in a .rail-frame grid (same
    columns + sticky as NodeHomeView's .node-layout); useSchoolsRail.ts resolves the tree
  railed_flat_routes: [schools-dashboard, teachers, students, classes, class-detail,
    analytics, settings]
  per_role:
    school_admin: server rail for their school node (/api/groups/:id/home, shared through
      nodeHomeCache — a flat<->node hop paints one identical tree); class pages recentre
      the rail on the class node
    teacher: node endpoints 403 teachers (scope = own classes, founder ruling 2026-07-30),
      so the rail builds from /api/me/teaching-context — the school as a NON-INTERACTIVE
      ancestor row (RailRef.inert), own classes as rows opening /schools/classes/:id;
      a groupless teacher (derived tutor) roots at "Your classes"
    legacy_no_node_rows: ineligible — flat views stay full-width as before
  rail_props: NodeMapRail gained RailRef.path (navigate to a flat page instead of the
    node home), RailRef.inert (orientation-only row, no click affordance) and a member
    prop (flat paths sit outside /schools/org, so path detection alone would show the
    admin escape)
  stability: the frame and its ONE rail instance persist across flat-view hops (only the
    main pane swaps); flat<->node hops paint the same cached tree synchronously
  tests: useSchoolsRail.test.ts

school_admin_first_run:  # fixed 2026-08-06 (Chepstow production inspection)
  why: |
    Nav unification (2026-07-30) redirects a school-scoped school_admin from
    /schools to /org/:schoolId — THIS page. Their two first-run affordances
    still lived only on DashboardView, so a real head teacher three weeks in
    had no route to the guided setup wizard (which has no nav tab) and no way
    to correct a school name someone else guessed for her: THE VIEW's Rename
    verb is `!member`. Both now render here too.
  gating: |
    isOwnSchoolNode = member mount AND isSchoolAdmin AND route :id equals the
    caller's own currentSchool.id. Never a class node, never a group, never
    the ssi_admin read-view mount.
      - setup banner: + payload loaded AND node.rollup.learnerCount === 0.
        ZERO PUPILS is the not-onboarded signal, never zero classes; one
        enrolled student retires it, so a running school is never nagged.
      - confirm-name card: + currentSchool.name_confirmed === false; saves
        via useSchoolData.confirmSchoolName (POST /api/school/update-profile,
        caller-scoped), then refetches schools AND the node home so the
        identity header stops showing the old name.
  data: |
    No new fetch and no payload change — currentSchool is already warm here
    because SchoolsContainer prefetches it and this node home renders inside
    that container. useSchoolData() resolves the schools Supabase client
    eagerly and THROWS when unset, so the call is wrapped: an unset client
    (possible on the admin mounts) degrades to "no first-run cards", which is
    the correct behaviour there anyway, rather than crashing the page.

navigation_rules:  # THE-VIEW §2
  - clicking any node NAME anywhere in admin lands on that node's HOME
  - Structure stays the quick-actions flyout; its open/see-progress verbs land on node home
  - old URLs live, old designs die (group summary, Full-schools list, admin ClassDetail shell)

components:
  - packages/player-vue/src/views/admin/NodeHomeView.vue
  - packages/player-vue/src/views/admin/AdminClassHome.vue
  - packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/NodeMapRail.vue
  - packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/NodeChildrenList.vue

tests:
  - packages/player-vue/src/views/admin/NodeHomeView.test.ts   # same grammar at 4 levels; lens filters; name-click pin
  - packages/player-vue/src/views/admin/NodeHomeView.schoolAdminFirstRun.test.ts  # setup banner + confirm-name card, own school node only
  - api/groups/[id]/home.test.ts                               # id resolution, rail, rollups, lenses, leader trimming

out_of_scope: |
  The LEADER member path converges on this grammar via the member mount
  (route_member above, 2026-07-20), and a school-scoped school_admin has
  landed here since the 2026-07-30 nav unification (their first-run
  affordances followed on 2026-08-06 — see school_admin_first_run). The
  remaining flat /schools views (TeacherDashboard, DashboardView's teacher
  and legacy no-school school_admin branches, ClassDetail) still converge in
  a later scoped pass.
  Class co-teacher MEMBERSHIP mutations are another worker's piece; here the
  teachers list renders read-only from class_teachers + the lead pointer.
